WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:06.249
The SCP Foundation is well aware of the thin
line separating itself between normalcy and

00:00:06.249 --> 00:00:08.540
the end of the human race.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:13.640
How easily that balance can be upset, and
the Foundation overturned.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.760
Without the Foundation, we may be subject
to any number of scenarios that may result

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.180
in our untimely extinction.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.300
The reign of the Scarlet King, ready to enslave
the world once more.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.970
The assimilation of the Broken God, and ascension
of humanity into a most perfect machine.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:36.190
The SCP Foundation is often outmatched and
outnumbered, competing against ancient, unspeakable

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:37.190
horrors.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.300
But those anomalies are well known.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.180
One could almost say that they’re built
up, and that the Foundation knows the risks

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.360
that can lie ahead in the future.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.539
In other words, they have time to prepare.

00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:52.780
But when dealing with the anomalous, the unexpected
is bound to occur.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.500
It’s part of what the SCP Foundation deals
with, and an element of their work they’ve

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.600
forever been unable to control or predict.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.510
The anomalous is untamed, it occurs without
rhyme or reason.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:09.720
In the world of the SCP Foundation, it’s
entirely possible you might wake up and find

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:15.840
that everyone around you has died, or that
the world’s been consumed by an evil, unseen

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:16.840
force.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.940
And there would be nothing you can do about
it.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:22.860
It happened, and not even the Foundation was
able to stop it.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.080
Perhaps the overabundance and unpredictability
of the world is why the Foundation deemed

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:34.170
it necessary to build SCP-2000, the machine
capable of restarting civilization from scratch.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:39.960
Death and mass destruction is always at the
door of the Foundation, and sometimes they’re

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.480
unable to prevent it.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.930
We’ve previously looked at the tale of Pietro
Wilson, who found himself in a world devastated

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.720
by an unknown entity.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:53.120
But SCP-5000 is far from the only time the
Foundation has dealt with the anomalous apocalypse.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:02:01.390
Today, we’re going to be telling the story
of SCP-1915, and an entity known only as the

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.390
Absence.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.590
It’s a story you may not have heard before,
and like all stories involving the SCP Foundation

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:10.790
and the End of the World, we look forward
to telling it.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:15.060
For centuries, civilizations have been predicting
the end of the world, from the mayans to the

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.560
ancient greeks to the biblical end-is-nigh
preachers of today, humanity seems obsessed

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.480
with trying to figure out the when and how
of its extinction.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:30.720
But when the date eventually comes, we all
find ourselves in the exact same place, healthy

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.870
and alive.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:36.730
None of us actually expect such an event to
happen, and if it did, most of us realize

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.420
that we wouldn’t be among the survivors
who could witness the world after it was empty.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:46.010
But for SCP-1915, that was not the case.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:51.000
SCP-1915 stood alone in the desert, listening
to the silence of the evening sunset.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.610
If he hadn’t known what had happened to
the world, he could call the scene beautiful,

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.900
or serene.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.650
He might find it pure.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:03.770
But he couldn’t allow himself to enjoy the
calming vistas, not after what he had witnessed.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.490
He knew what lies beneath and among the sands
of that desert.

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:12.731
He knew the feeling of seven billion human
souls being ground up, stretched thin, and

00:03:12.731 --> 00:03:16.180
buried below without any trace of their existence
remaining.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:20.320
And he knew this because he was the one who
put them there.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.330
“It's quiet out here.”

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.070
SCP-1915 thought to himself.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.410
“Oh, brother.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.800
It all happens so fast, once we're gone.”

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.310
But let’s turn back the clock a bit.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.090
Who is SCP-1915?

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.550
How did he get himself into this situation?

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:39.270
The Foundation’s database holds the answers.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:44.190
SCP-1915 was a humanoid entity contained in
a standard humanoid chamber, which it had

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.280
modified itself.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:51.910
SCP-1915’s containment procedures stated
that furniture and sustenance were unnecessary,

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.980
as SCP-1915 provided both of them itself.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.550
SCP-1915 looked like a completely average,
middle-aged white male.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.620
The type you’d pass by on the street and
neglect to notice.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:09.310
He was of unexceptional build and height,
and public records gave him an equally unexceptional

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:14.060
name, which has been lost due to years of
the Foundation’s redaction and information

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.060
suppression.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:20.650
Thankfully for the Foundation, a background
check into SCP-1915’s civilian life revealed

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:27.910
no friends or relatives, meaning that removing
SCP-1915 from society was as easy as it first

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:28.910
appeared.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.670
SCP-1915 is, so far, relatively unremarkable.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:35.810
And that’s entirely the point.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:40.810
SCP-1915’s anomalous nature lies in its
ability to prevent any significant, long-term

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:45.510
change to its body, personality, memory, or
lifestyle.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:50.889
SCP-1915 is also a reality bender, and it
will actively alter the world around it to

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:56.330
maintain its personal status quo, though these
alterations are largely limited to non-living

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.610
matter manipulation and mental manipulations.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:05.810
As far as reality benders go, SCP-1915 is
relatively weak, as it is unable to permanently

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:10.260
affect living creatures with its anomalous
abilities other than itself.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:16.380
What makes SCP-1915 especially interesting,
and especially dangerous as well, is the fact

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.040
that it is entirely unaware of its own anomalous
nature.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:25.110
It’s mild discontent expressed in interviews
with the Foundation suggested to the organization

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:30.830
that SCP-1915 has little, if any control over
its own abilities.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:36.890
SCP-1915 is, due to its anomalous nature,
entirely unaware of its containment, as being

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:42.370
locked up by the SCP Foundation would definitely
be a significant, long-term change.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:47.370
In fact, it still believes that it is employed
by a corporation, and working a mundane office

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:52.340
job, where the Foundation recovered SCP-1915
originally.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:58.449
SCP-1915 cannot bring itself to accept its
situation, and has instead unconsciously altered

00:05:58.449 --> 00:06:01.479
its mind and containment cell accordingly.

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:06.280
To SCP-1915, absolutely nothing has changed.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:12.210
During its initial recovery from its office
job, SCP-1915 altered the Mobile Task Force’s

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:16.870
armored vehicle into a city bus, and convinced
itself that the operatives escorting it were

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:20.110
simply other civilians on their commute to
work.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:26.500
Once it arrived at Site-17, SCP-1915 converted
its containment cell into an exact replica

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:32.020
of its apartment, complete with electronic
devices akin to the ones it owned, running

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:33.870
water, and sewage access.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.139
It even assumed the other researchers and
guards inside the facility were neighbors,

00:06:38.139 --> 00:06:39.820
or local service workers.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:45.720
The morning following its containment, SCP-1915
left its cell, despite it being locked, and

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.420
entered a maintenance closet.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:53.389
The closet was transformed into a re-creation
of the office cubicle SCP-1915 worked in prior

00:06:53.389 --> 00:06:54.910
to being contained.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:07:00.759
When Foundation researchers tried to communicate
with SCP-1915, it apologized for "coming after

00:07:00.759 --> 00:07:05.300
hours to finish the budget report", claiming
that it needed the extra income.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:11.080
During an interview with the Foundation, SCP-1915
still couldn’t accept its situation.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:17.790
Instead, it believed that it was being referred
to by name, despite being referred to as SCP-1915,

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.940
and that it was still working an office job.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:24.690
It displayed remorse that it was passed over
for a promotion yet again, and asked the interviewer

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:28.440
if it was working on the “third floor”.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:33.910
SCP-1915 was completely and utterly unable
to view reality outside of its own lens.

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:37.770
Sure, he’s able to alter reality, but he’s
entirely unaware of it.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:43.490
In a way, the only thing keeping SCP-1915
chained to that soul-sucking office job is

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:47.080
itself, and its inability to accept anything
different.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.669
What a metaphor, right?

00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:53.729
But how could SCP-1915 defy reality in the
face of the world ending?

00:07:53.729 --> 00:07:57.720
Would he still believe that he’s working
away at a budget report or grabbing coffee

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:00.270
for his boss when the world’s burning around
him?

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:06.600
Let’s move back to the desert scene, where
SCP-1915 is standing before an empty world,

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:11.259
seemingly holding itself responsible for ridding
the earth of humanity.

00:08:11.259 --> 00:08:15.540
SCP-1915 recollects what occurred, the events
leading up to this moment.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:20.820
He thinks of what happened when staring outside
the windows of its containment cell-apartment.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:23.460
SCP-1915 remembers what it saw.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:28.170
“It began the day you, you that I have never
known, found my power.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:32.919
The power I hid from myself in some previous
life, for reasons I can now easily guess.

00:08:32.919 --> 00:08:38.300
I was looking out of the window of my apartment,
so I could see the stars, and instead I saw

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:43.819
you, blazing as you tore yourself asunder
to keep the power away from yourself.

00:08:43.819 --> 00:08:47.809
You didn't trust what you would do with it,
and so you chose to throw it away.

00:08:47.809 --> 00:08:52.649
You knew yourself all too well, as I suspect
I did too, at one point.

00:08:52.649 --> 00:08:57.420
By all accounts, I should not have been able
to see you, for my apartment was truly a tiny

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:02.339
containment cell about half a mile underground,
but such considerations never meant much to

00:09:02.339 --> 00:09:04.649
one living entirely in his own world.

00:09:04.649 --> 00:09:10.589
When I saw the moment of your demise, I became
aware of myself for the first time in…

00:09:10.589 --> 00:09:13.209
I have no idea in how long.

00:09:13.209 --> 00:09:18.339
Whichever part of me that led me to throw
away my power did the same to my will, trapping

00:09:18.339 --> 00:09:22.399
it in an eternal status quo from which there
could be no release.

00:09:22.399 --> 00:09:27.870
An eternity of filling spreadsheets for employers
who existed solely in my head, of nine o'clock

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:32.170
meetings with no one, of fake crushes over
imaginary women.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.860
An eternity of tired, grinding mediocrity.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:39.779
But that was over that night, with your soul
burning in the atmosphere like the loneliest

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:40.879
of stars.

00:09:40.879 --> 00:09:41.959
I awakened.

00:09:41.959 --> 00:09:42.959
I died.”

00:09:42.959 --> 00:09:49.139
Whatever SCP-1915 saw that day made it aware
of the farce of a life it had created for

00:09:49.139 --> 00:09:50.139
itself.

00:09:50.139 --> 00:09:53.629
And beneath those feelings of conformity,
there was sadness.

00:09:53.629 --> 00:09:57.209
“For whatever left that little cell-turned
apartment wasn't me anymore.

00:09:57.209 --> 00:10:02.779
I was never more than an earthworm, distinct
from all the rest only in that I had a little

00:10:02.779 --> 00:10:05.410
more control over the soil in which I crawled.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:10.930
They never thought me more than a minor reality
bender, a bundle of introverted powers and

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:15.339
neurosis that was very unlikely to ever pose
any serious threat.

00:10:15.339 --> 00:10:16.350
And they were right.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:23.160
The person I was, SCP-1915, as they called
me, never was anything other than that.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:27.100
But 1915 died that day, watching a fallen
star.”

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:32.589
Realizing it had been cheated, lied to, and
the crushing reality of its current situation,

00:10:32.589 --> 00:10:36.209
SCP-1915 lashed out against the Foundation.

00:10:36.209 --> 00:10:40.430
“The thing that then swatted the guards
posted at its cell like they were less than

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:46.869
gnats, that razed Site-17 into this fine white
sand that is now so warm beneath the feet,

00:10:46.869 --> 00:10:48.089
that was something else.

00:10:48.089 --> 00:10:53.230
Not an entity, for that would imply a personality,
and this thing surely has none.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:58.339
Not a purpose, for there was no purpose behind
its action then, nor will there be for any

00:10:58.339 --> 00:11:00.089
of its actions to come.

00:11:00.089 --> 00:11:03.140
Nor was it a will, for it wants nothing.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:08.069
Not vengeance, not dominion, not freedom,
not even simple power.

00:11:08.069 --> 00:11:14.499
No, if I had to describe that thing as anything
at all, it would be an… an absence.

00:11:14.499 --> 00:11:17.129
A void where the entity should be.

00:11:17.129 --> 00:11:18.499
A lack of purpose.

00:11:18.499 --> 00:11:21.930
An imbecile force devoid of all will.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:23.339
An Absence.”

00:11:23.339 --> 00:11:28.259
SCP-1915 had, in its realization, become an
Absence.

00:11:28.259 --> 00:11:32.860
Perhaps realizing the meaninglessness of its
own-self-contained life, it took out that

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.249
absence of feeling onto the world.

00:11:35.249 --> 00:11:40.560
And with SCP-1915’s absence came humanity’s
absence as well.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:47.179
Like nothing had ever happened, SCP-1915 had
created an absence of humanity.

00:11:47.179 --> 00:11:51.820
It had erased everything but the sun, the
desert, and itself.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:55.730
And now it stood alone in an empty, lonely
world.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:12:00.860
It continued to think to itself, remembering
how it caused the downfall of the SCP Foundation

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:01.999
so easily.

00:12:01.999 --> 00:12:06.499
“After Site-17's destruction, retaliation
soon followed.

00:12:06.499 --> 00:12:10.559
Standard containment teams at first, though
certainly still enough to meet any anomaly

00:12:10.559 --> 00:12:15.250
the Foundation imagined could be contained
in Site-17 with overwhelming force.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:20.279
When those men failed to return, failed to
even report their arrival, more serious measures

00:12:20.279 --> 00:12:21.759
had to be taken.

00:12:21.759 --> 00:12:25.709
Site-17 has always been isolated, and so they
could act freely.

00:12:25.709 --> 00:12:31.079
Gunships and fire teams, aerial bombardment
and artillery barrages, the Foundation came

00:12:31.079 --> 00:12:37.660
down on what it still believed to be SCP-1915
like a fire god's fist, all heat and sound

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:38.809
and bluster.

00:12:38.809 --> 00:12:43.029
Had it still been truly corporeal, I doubt
even ashes would have remained.

00:12:43.029 --> 00:12:47.779
But whatever the Absence truly was by that
point, the tattered semblance of my flesh

00:12:47.779 --> 00:12:50.829
hanging around it had very little to do with
it.

00:12:50.829 --> 00:12:57.189
It simply stood there and took it all in,
and the Foundation's initial fury was soon…

00:12:57.189 --> 00:12:58.189
spent.

00:12:58.189 --> 00:13:01.139
It then began to walk, and not too quickly
either.

00:13:01.139 --> 00:13:06.420
For days, it simply leisurely strode on while
the Foundation threw everything it had at

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:07.420
it.

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:13.209
I watched from within my deadbolt as it walked
unfeeling, uncaring, and this desert followed

00:13:13.209 --> 00:13:18.139
in its wake, as inscrutable and unstoppable
as its harbinger.”

00:13:18.139 --> 00:13:22.809
While the Foundation, and the rest of humanity,
were decimated quite easily, there were some

00:13:22.809 --> 00:13:27.889
immortal beings that SCP-1915 was aware it
could not fully erase.

00:13:27.889 --> 00:13:30.939
Other anomalies that the Foundation had contained
somewhat.

00:13:30.939 --> 00:13:36.059
But they were all but remained, tied to a
dead and desolate world.

00:13:36.059 --> 00:13:38.279
SCP-1915’s memories continued.

00:13:38.279 --> 00:13:43.559
“When someone walks, they are bound to reach
somewhere eventually, despite everyone's best

00:13:43.559 --> 00:13:49.290
efforts, and so the Absence arrived at its
first city, the sands at its heels like an

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:50.510
obedient lapdog.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:55.079
Oh, there have been villages and towns before
that, but the Absence didn't seem to care

00:13:55.079 --> 00:13:56.509
enough to bother with them.

00:13:56.509 --> 00:14:02.379
It simply walked by, leaving them to the whims
of the sands, which were only ever singular

00:14:02.379 --> 00:14:03.579
in their intent.

00:14:03.579 --> 00:14:08.449
But through the streets of the city it strode,
as Mobile Task Forces fought and fell to buy

00:14:08.449 --> 00:14:12.389
the civilian population just a few more minutes
to evacuate.

00:14:12.389 --> 00:14:17.480
By this point, hiding what was truly going
on became impossible, of course, as street

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:20.920
after street sank beneath that gentle crawling
tide.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:24.449
The Foundation had of course attempted to
evacuate the city once it realized there would

00:14:24.449 --> 00:14:31.149
be no stopping the Absence, but if I've learned
anything in my… eons as a corporate peon,

00:14:31.149 --> 00:14:36.041
is that organizing an operation of that magnitude
is something that takes a lot more time than

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:37.249
the Foundation had.

00:14:37.249 --> 00:14:40.480
It's a wonder they managed to save as many
as they did.”

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:49.149
City to city, town to town, SCP-1915 continued
on a warpath, turning its surroundings to

00:14:49.149 --> 00:14:50.149
dust.

00:14:50.149 --> 00:14:52.869
The earth became the desert that it now stood
in.

00:14:52.869 --> 00:14:58.579
In one moment, a city of five hundred thousand
existed, and in the next, it didn’t.

00:14:58.579 --> 00:15:00.970
SCP-1915 could not explain it.

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:04.179
Instead, it simply was, and was not.

00:15:04.179 --> 00:15:07.749
The Foundation, as SCP-1915 recalled, was
becoming desperate.

00:15:07.749 --> 00:15:11.720
And it began to turn to various groups of
interest for help.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:16.369
“It was then, I believe, that the Foundation
realized it could not stand alone.

00:15:16.369 --> 00:15:21.749
The next few months of the Absence's march
saw them turn to their sometimes allies; Coalition

00:15:21.749 --> 00:15:26.589
Magekillers and thermonuclear strikes, Initiative
Paladins and holy relics.

00:15:26.589 --> 00:15:33.439
Sniper rifle or sacred sword, burning inferno
or divine retribution, the Absence did not

00:15:33.439 --> 00:15:34.439
care.

00:15:34.439 --> 00:15:37.440
And soon, the Foundation had no allies left
to turn to.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:43.480
It then called on its once vicious enemies;
Ink Eaters wove their art in maddening patterns,

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:45.389
to break the minds of the infinite.

00:15:45.389 --> 00:15:49.879
Archivists and Librarians poured from the
Ways, bringing with them the knowledge of

00:15:49.879 --> 00:15:52.230
a hundred thousand worlds.

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:56.939
Clockwork Titans shook the barren whiteness
of the sands with the thunder of metal.

00:15:56.939 --> 00:15:58.540
The Absence did not care.

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.259
And soon, the Foundation ran out of enemies.

00:16:01.259 --> 00:16:05.709
In an act of desperation, they then committed
their most painful betrayal.

00:16:05.709 --> 00:16:08.819
The wardens unleashed upon the world their
prisoners.

00:16:08.819 --> 00:16:12.809
Of these, I have made note, though I doubt
the Absence did the same.”

00:16:12.809 --> 00:16:17.329
With the anomalous objects it once contained
now released, the Foundation used its own

00:16:17.329 --> 00:16:23.910
SCP objects against SCP-1915 in an effort
to stop the entity from destroying the world

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.110
itself.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:32.629
SCP-1915 recalled fighting against SCP-073
and SCP-076, the brothers Cain and Able.

00:16:32.629 --> 00:16:38.769
It recalled SCP-343, the entity claiming to
be the Abrhamaic God, launching an assault

00:16:38.769 --> 00:16:42.129
of earth-shattering destruction and divine
wrath.

00:16:42.129 --> 00:16:47.389
But SCP-343, nor the brothers, were able to
match SCP-1915.

00:16:47.389 --> 00:16:53.279
When they stared into SCP-1915’s lack of
a gaze, they all faded into nothing, much

00:16:53.279 --> 00:16:57.939
like the rest of the world that turned to
dust as a result of the Absence.

00:16:57.939 --> 00:17:05.000
SCP-1915 then recalled encountering two forms
of SCP-2845, the God Pangloss.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.690
Both of which were powerful, mighty, and all
consuming.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:15.000
But they had form, and their being knelt before
SCP-1915 like everything else did.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:20.310
The absence withstood their presence, like
it had done with everything before them.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:26.630
For years, the Foundation continued to send
every anomaly in its possession after SCP-1915.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:30.290
But they paled in comparison to the power
of the Absence.

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:34.300
And eventually, the Foundation was out of
anomalies.

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:38.550
The Foundation was out of time, as well.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:43.550
SCP-1915’s march to the ends of the earth
brought it to a single remaining human settlement.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:48.480
A coalition of survivors that had couped themselves
up in hopes of outrunning the entity.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:52.860
Some were former agents of the Foundation,
others were members of various Groups of Interest.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:58.410
But, as you might have expected, they didn’t
hold a candle to SCP-1915.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:04.260
In an act of defiance against the world that
it had been keeping itself from, SCP-1915

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.590
wiped the city from the earth.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:09.190
And then, it was truly alone.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:15.180
And now all SCP-1915 had to do was think back
to what had occurred, and how much longer

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:20.330
the rest of the universe had before it too,
succumbed to the Absence.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:27.110
“Quiet, small, bereft of heroics and great
deeds, free of pretensions of great meaning.

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:30.020
One night, there was human race on the planet
Earth.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:31.020
The next, there wasn't.

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:35.520
And that was that.The stars did not wait for
you, brother.

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:41.820
When you took my power, when you burned yourself
in the skies above, they looked upon you and

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:42.910
felt nothing.

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:47.710
The stars did not wait for humanity, for all
of the promise it showed, for all of the promise

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:48.970
others saw in them.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.670
But what of the Absence?

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:51.790
What of me?

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:58.000
We are, I am, by all accounts and possible
qualifications, the greatest monster this

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.600
world has ever saw.

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:01.580
Perhaps that any world saw.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:05.310
And yet, brother, I see now that the stars
wait for us.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.310
For me.

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:08.450
Where is the justice in that?

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.450
Seek it not, for there is none.

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:12.640
But the fact remains, brother.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:14.850
The stars do not wait for you.

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:16.550
But they wait for me.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.960
To take them into my embrace.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.050
I suspect I shall not be long.”

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:26.950
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The World's
Gone Beautiful” and “SCP XK Class End

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:32.240
of the World Scenarios Explained” for more
end of the world SCP stories to help you prep

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:32.740
for the end of times!

